## Diagram 2 — The Adapter Pattern

> **Used on:** Architecture Overview, Philosophy page  
> **Type:** Side-by-side comparison  

### Left side: "Without Abstraction"

```
┌──────────────┐
│ Your App     │
└──────┬───────┘
       │  tightly coupled
┌──────┴───────┐
│ Platform API │
│ (name,       │
│  regular_    │
│  price...)   │
└──────────────┘
```

- Red dashed border or ✗ badge
- Label: **Vendor Lock-In**

### Right side: "With Commerce.js"

```
┌──────────────┐
│ Your App     │  ← writes once
└──────┬───────┘
       │
┌──────┴───────┐
│   Unified    │  ← portable interface
│  Interface   │
└──────┬───────┘
       │
┌──────┴───────┐
│   Adapter    │  ← swappable
└──────┬───────┘
       │
┌──────┴───────┐
│  Any Platform│
│ Salla │ Shopify │ Custom
└──────────────┘
```

- Green border or ✓ badge
- Label: **Platform Freedom**

### Key message

Arrow between the two sides: "Same app code, different backend"

